==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|æŋkə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[spank]]s.
# An [[instrument]] used to give someone a spanking or spank, such as a [[paddle]].
# {{label|en|nautical}} A [[fore]] and [[aft]] [[gaff]]-rigged [[sail]] on the aft-most mast of a square-rigged vessel.
#: {{rfquotek|Totten}}
# {{label|en|dated|music}} A [[musician]] who plays his instrument well.
# {{label|en|obsolete|UK|dialect}} A small [[coin]].
#* '''1772''', ''The Town and Country Magazine'' (volume 4, page 344)
#*: Egad, Jack, I am glad to see you, for I want a few '''spankers'''.
# {{label|en|dated}} One who takes long, quick strides in walking.
# {{label|en|dated}} A swift horse.
# {{label|en|dated}} Something very large, or larger than usual; a [[whopper]].

